    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task: on a successful owner create, emit an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger carrying the owner id, `customerCode` and `registrationDate`.\n\nI implemented this as a small, cohesive unit to keep structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New function class** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 a single-method OfficeFloor step (CC=1, no surrounding class complexity) that reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val` and logs to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`:\n   ```\n   AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-01\n   ```\n\n2. **Wired it into `owners.POST.yml`** between `save` (which assigns the id) and `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours.\n\nRather than modifying `SaveOwner` or `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (which would grow an existing method/class), I added the behaviour as an isolated step \u2014 so no existing function's complexity or line count changes. The audit fires after the id is generated and only on the success path, since any earlier escalation (duplicate, quota, invalid telephone) short-circuits the pipeline before reaching it.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreLogsAuditOnCreate` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
